# raw Reddit files #
############
*.zst

# processed Reddit files #
############
*.csv
*.jsonl
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# Atomic-write temp files from the pipeline (e.g. .RC_2014-12.csv.b8cWe1).
# These escape the *.csv / *.jsonl rules because the real extension is the
# random suffix; they are renamed to their final name on completion.
.*.csv.*
.*.jsonl.*
.*.sqlite.*
.*.sqlite3.*

# The author map — NEVER commit. It holds the username -> anonymous ID
# mapping that organize_anonymize and warm_author_map build, so it is the one
# artifact that can re-identify every author in the corpus. SQLite's
# write-ahead log and shared-memory sidecars hold the same content and do not
# match the extension rules above, so they are listed explicitly.
data/user_map.sqlite3
*.sqlite-wal
*.sqlite-shm
*.sqlite3-wal
*.sqlite3-shm

# Whitelist the relevance training samples and the post-filter QA samples so
# reviewers can audit the FPR / kappa / classifier-performance claims.
!data/data_relevance_ratings/**/*.csv
!data/data_relevance_QAratings/**/*.csv

# Local-only de-identification artifacts for the QA samples — NEVER commit.
# Keys map the blinded random_id back to author/id/metadata; backups are the
# pre-anonymization originals. Both still contain the stripped PII.
data/data_relevance_QAratings_keys/
data/data_relevance_QAratings_ORIGINAL_BACKUP/

# trained models #
# NOTE: `models/*` rather than `models/` so the two training-split directories
# below can be re-included. Git cannot re-include anything under a directory
# that is itself excluded, so the wildcard form is required here.
models/*

# Ship the train/validation/test splits behind the released classifiers, so the
# reported held-out performance can be reproduced. These are NOT regenerable:
# train_relevance.py recreates a split when they are absent, but its ordering
# comes from unsorted iteration over a set of integer doc ids, which is stable
# within one CPython build and not across versions. Both contain post text and
# are covered by the licensing note in README.md, not by the MIT License.
!models/train_relevance_data_split/
!models/train_relevance_data_split/**
!models/train_moralization_data_split/
!models/train_moralization_data_split/**

# pycache #
code/__pycache__

# Slurm job stdout/stderr per-task logs #
slurm_logs/

# HF publishing tooling: ship the sources, not the generated artifacts.
# The zip is a duplicate snapshot of isaac_hf/ and will drift from it; the
# preview HTML is regenerated from performance.py.
isaac-hf-publish/isaac_hf_deliverable.zip
isaac-hf-publish/isaac_hf/performance_tab_preview.html

# Byte-compiled files anywhere (the code/ rule above predates other packages).
__pycache__/
*.pyc
